# Required-review routing (see GOVERNANCE.md and CONTRIBUTING.md's "Review and merge policy").
# GitHub requests a review from every owner matching a changed path, and branch protection on
# `main` requires that review before a pull request can merge -- including the founding
# maintainer's own pull requests, since branch protection here has no admin bypass.
#
# GitHub never counts a PR author's own approval, so listing only one name here would make that
# person's own pull requests permanently unmergeable -- both current collaborators are listed for
# exactly that reason: whichever one of you didn't open the PR is the one who can approve it.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so keep the repo-wide default first and any narrower
# path-specific line after it, per GitHub's own documented CODEOWNERS precedence.

